Package: slim-scan
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-osd
Suggests: ocrmypdf, sane-utils, slim-scan-gui
Description: scan all pages from a document feeder into one PDF
 slim-scan scans every page in a scanner's document feeder into a single
 PDF. It talks to network scanners over WSD (built in) or to any scanner
 SANE supports, through scanimage.
 .
 It removes blank pages, finds the paper size, straightens and turns pages
 upright, and can add a searchable text layer with Tesseract or OCRmyPDF.
 It was developed against the Epson ES-580W.
 .
 This package contains the slim-scan command. The desktop app is in
 slim-scan-gui.

Package: slim-scan-gui
Architecture: all
Depends: slim-scan (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3 (>= 3.9),
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.12),
         gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: scan documents from a network scanner into PDF files (desktop app)
 Slim Scan is a GTK 4 / libadwaita app built on slim-scan. It scans every
 page in a scanner's document feeder into one PDF, shows the pages for
 review and correction before saving, and can make the PDF searchable.
 .
 It can stay in the status bar and start at login.
